==================================================
HSRP VERIFICATION
==================================================

Run on GW1 and GW2:

show standby
show standby brief
show ip interface brief

EXPECTED INITIAL STATUS:

GW1:
State: Standby
Physical IP: 192.168.1.1
Virtual IP: 192.168.1.3

GW2:
State: Active
Physical IP: 192.168.1.2
Virtual IP: 192.168.1.3

Both routers have default priority 100.
GW2 wins the tie because its interface IP is higher.

==================================================
FAILOVER TESTING
==================================================

STEP 1: Check HSRP status.

show standby brief

STEP 2: Simulate GW2 failure.

On GW2:

enable
configure terminal
interface FastEthernet0/0
shutdown
exit

STEP 3: Verify GW1.

On GW1:

show standby brief

EXPECTED RESULT:
GW1 should become Active.

STEP 4: Test PC connectivity.

From PC0:

ping 192.168.1.3

STEP 5: Restore GW2.

On GW2:

configure terminal
interface FastEthernet0/0
no shutdown
exit

STEP 6: Verify HSRP status again.

show standby brief

NOTE:
Without preemption configured, GW1 may remain Active after GW2 recovers.

